r it's going to be profitable in some  way i might get paid speaking gigs or  whatever the case may be now here's what  i can say about that  i'm going to give you a list of people  that i know are not  grifters and what i mean by that is  whether we agree or disagree  on any particular issue what you see  them say  publicly lines up completely with what  they say privately they are not playing  characters  they're not calculating their positions  for how it's going to be perceived by  their audiences or  for profitability and the reason i'm  able to give you this list  is because i know both these people's uh  public  work as well as knowing them privately  as individuals  and in no particular order here are  people that are not grifters  jenkin anna from the young turks i've  known them both for a long time  if you talk to them privately what they  say is exactly what they say on their  show  we don't have to agree about everything  surely i'd have differences with them  about for example the  israeli-palestinian conflict but  they are totally sincere in what they  say and what they believe would be best  for the world  i am totally sincere in what i say there  is no grift or calculation there  great okay sam cedar from the majority  report i've been to what must be at this  point 15 or 20 conferences with sam over  the years where we spend hours together  every political conversation i've had  with sam and that i've heard  and overheard sam have with other folks  including people from the revolutionary  left etc  the public sam and the private sam is  exactly the same person no grift  kyle kalinski i've hung out with kyle um  and i've talked to kyle a ton over the  years the kyle you see on his  youtube channel as far as i know and  again i don't watch a lot of this stuff  online  it's the same kyle that i know privately  farron cousins from ring of fire is the  same guy  politically privately as he is publicly  nomiki from the no mickey show i've  known her for 